    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46937" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sup-par</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subpar</span></b> ), păris, adj.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>nearly
			equal</i> (rare but class.): huic aetati suppares Alcibiades,
			Critias, * <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut. 7, 29</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aetas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vell.
					1, 17, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aevum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 1, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">musicae suppari gressu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 6, p. 183, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fratres, nec similes ejus nec suppares,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 26, 10, 9</span></i>
			. — 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">In logic: propositiones suppares,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 3, p. 31 sq.</span></i>
			</div>
